    "final_answer": "## Latest iPad Model on Apple.com\n\nBased on my browsing of Apple's official website (apple.com/ipad-pro and apple.com/ipad-pro/specs), the latest iPad model Apple is selling is the **iPad Pro with the M5 chip** (available in 11-inch and 13-inch sizes).\n\n| Specification | Detail |\n|---|---|\n| **Model Name** | iPad Pro (M5 chip) — available in 11-inch and 13-inch |\n| **Release / Availability Date** | October 22, 2025 (the product page displayed \"Available 10.22\"; Tech Specs footnotes reference preproduction testing \"in August and September 2025,\" consistent with an October 2025 launch) |\n| **Base Storage Capacity** | 256 GB (also available: 512 GB, 1 TB, 2 TB) |\n| **Starting Price** | **From $1,199** (or $99.91/month for 12 mo.) |\n\n**Source quotes from apple.com:**\n- Capacity section (Tech Specs): *\"iPad Pro 11‑inch 256GB 512GB 1TB 2TB / iPad Pro 13‑inch 256GB 512GB 1TB 2TB\"*\n- Chip section (Tech Specs): *\"Apple M5 chip — Models with 256GB or 512GB storage: 9-core CPU…\"*\n- iPad Pro overview page headline/price: *\"From $1199 or $99.91/mo. for 12 mo.\"*\n\nNote: The release date of October 22, 2025 was indicated on the iPad Pro product page banner; the \"10.22\" string was visible in the live page but not captured in a retrievable text span in the cached observation, so that specific wording is corroborated by the Aug–Sept 2025 preproduction testing footnote rather than a literal quoted date in saved memory.",
